 {
   bool success = true;
+#ifdef ACE_WASI
+  // Nothing to configure, and nothing lost by not configuring it.
+  //
+  // RECVPKTINFO asks the stack to attach the datagram's DESTINATION address to
+  // each receive as ancillary data, which matters on a multi-homed host that
+  // binds the wildcard address. On wasm32-wasip2 it cannot work and does not
+  // need to:
+  //
+  //   * wasi:sockets has no ancillary data. ACE's recvmsg here is supplied by
+  //     plugins/opendds/shim/wk-opendds-net.c over recvfrom, which sets
+  //     msg_controllen = 0, so no control message can ever arrive no matter
+  //     what the socket was asked for. ACE already falls back to
+  //     get_local_addr() in that case (SOCK_Dgram.cpp), which is the answer.
+  //   * a wk node is not multi-homed. It has exactly one address on the one
+  //     Network it is wired to (10.0.0.x / fd00::x, assigned by the host), so
+  //     the destination address of anything it receives is already known.
+  //
+  // ACE nevertheless defines ACE_RECVPKTINFO, because wasi-libc's
+  // <netinet/in.h> defines IP_PKTINFO as a CONSTANT while implementing none of
+  // it -- the same "the header says yes, the libc says no" split documented in
+  // ace/config-wasi.h -- so without this the setsockopt below is attempted,
+  // returns ENOTSUP, and Spdp treats it as fatal.
+  ACE_UNUSED_ARG(sock);
+  ACE_UNUSED_ARG(ipv4);
+  return true;
+#endif
 #if defined ACE_RECVPKTINFO || defined ACE_RECVPKTINFO6
   if (ipv4) {
